## 1. PURPOSE AND CANONICAL RULES

This document defines the canonical frontend routes, module ownership, homepage registry, shared systems, feature boundaries and implementation order for HOMIO.

It is a structural registry. A path listed as a target or planned capability is not proof that the file exists, the route works, inventory is live, or a test has passed.

### 1.1 Sources of truth

| Responsibility | Authority |
|---|---|
| Business/domain architecture | `REOS_CONTROL_CENTER/architecture/master/HOMIO_REOS_MASTER_ARCHITECTURE.json` |
| Project gate, active task and execution state | `REOS_CONTROL_CENTER/data/state.json` and the existing authorized Control Center |
| Approved frontend experience and UX boundaries | `REOS_CONTROL_CENTER/architecture/frontend/plans/HOMIO_FRONTEND_IMPLEMENTATION_BLUEPRINT.json` |
| Frontend module registry | This document |
| Frontend coordination manifest | `REOS_CONTROL_CENTER/architecture/frontend/plans/HOMIO_FRONTEND_EXECUTION_PLAN.json` |
| Committed frontend source | GitHub branch `reos-development` |
| Continuity and engineering-time repository intelligence | ACRL, outside normal frontend runtime |
| PS Output and other diagnostic snapshots | Evidence/diagnostics only; never execution authority |

If this registry conflicts with the approved REOS Master Architecture or canonical execution state, do not silently override the higher-authority source. Reconcile the conflict through the prescribed workflow before implementation.

### 1.2 Non-negotiable boundaries

1. Do not manually modify `REOS_CONTROL_CENTER/data/state.json` to manufacture a task transition or completion.
2. Do not import ACRL or `AUTONOMY_ENGINE` runtime modules into normal frontend runtime.
3. Do not read Control Center state as live consumer-facing application data.
4. Do not duplicate REOS business engines, canonical inventory, authorization, ownership, leads, deals, evidence, governance or commission logic in the frontend.
5. Do not invent live property inventory, prices, availability, verification, market statistics, API capabilities or backend connections.
6. Inspect existing source paths and imports before adding files. Reuse existing modules; do not create duplicates to match an outdated plan.
7. `src/app` owns route entry and page composition. `src/components` owns reusable UI and shell. `src/features` owns experience-specific implementation. `src/lib/reos` is a thin integration boundary.
8. A planned component or route is not considered implemented until the current Git tree and prescribed verification establish that fact.
9. The public HOMIO identity remains a premium global real-estate platform. The first active launch market is Pune; the two requirements are complementary, not contradictory.

