## 40. MARKET STRATEGY — GLOBAL BRAND, PUNE-FIRST LAUNCH

HOMIO's public identity remains a premium global real-estate platform. The first active launch experience is Pune-first.

These statements must be implemented together.

### 40.1 Initial launch behavior

The initial buyer-facing discovery experience prioritizes:

- Pune city and supported Pune localities.
- Buy and rent according to supported inventory.
- Residential properties and projects backed by authorized sources.
- Commercial/office/plot categories only to the degree that the related inventory and capability are ready.
- Natural-language and structured search.
- Clear property and project context.
- Save, compare, enquiry and visit paths that match the actual capabilities available.
- Trust, source and freshness signals only when supported by verified data.

Do not use Dubai, Singapore, Tokyo, London or New York as active default search suggestions, homepage city cards or unsupported market claims in the Pune launch experience.

Do not invent Pune listings, locality trends, project prices or inventory counts to make the initial experience look full.

### 40.2 Future market behavior

Future India and international markets remain part of the target platform architecture. They must be activated through explicit market configuration and readiness checks, not by merely adding a city name to a UI array.

The future experience may use separate localized market pages/routes. Each activated market should have an intentional locale, relevant currency/unit/address formatting, permitted source/inventory coverage, appropriate legal/content rules and route/SEO behavior.

Do not expose a crowded global city directory on the Pune homepage just to demonstrate future scalability.

### 40.3 Activation principle

```text
Market exists in architecture
        ≠
Market is live for users

Market appears in a card
        ≠
Verified inventory is available

Market activation
        requires
approved configuration + source/data readiness
+ route behavior + localization + verification
```

